-- title:
--   Level-constant degree-two Shapiro–Mackey surjectivity for coinduced modules
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a commutative ring, $V$ a $k$-module, $G$ a group, and write $\Gamma$ for the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$. Let $r \colon G \to \Gamma$ be a homomorphism and $U \trianglelefteq \Gamma$ a normal subgroup which is open in the sense assumed, namely that some intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$ has $F_0^{\mathrm{fix}} =$ its fixing subgroup contained in $U$. Put $T = \Gamma/(U \sqcup \mathrm{range}\,r)$ (the quotient by the subgroup generated by $U$ and the image of $r$) and $D = r^{-1}(U)$, and let $\gamma \colon T \to \Gamma$ be any set-theoretic section, i.e. $\gamma t$ lies in the class $t$ for every $t$. Let $b$ assign to each $t \in T$ a function $b_t \colon D \times D \to V$ lying in [`groupCohomology.levelCocycles₂`](def/GroupCohomology_ContinuousH2.html#L85) for the level map $r$ restricted to $D$ and the trivial $D$-representation on $V$; that is, each $b_t$ is an inhomogeneous $2$-cocycle which is level-constant with respect to $r$ (invariant, in each argument, under right translation by elements whose image under $r$ fixes some intermediate field finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$). The conclusion asserts the existence of $c \colon G \times G \to \mathrm{Res}_r\,\mathrm{CoInd}_{U}^{\Gamma}(V)$, where $V$ carries the trivial $U$-action and elements of the coinduced representation are realised as functions $\Gamma \to V$, such that $c$ lies in [`groupCohomology.levelCocycles₂`](def/GroupCohomology_ContinuousH2.html#L85) for $r$ and this $G$-representation, and such that $c(d,d')(\gamma t) = b_t(d,d')$ for all $t \in T$ and all $d, d' \in D$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half, at the level of level-constant (continuous) $2$-cocycles rather than cohomology classes, of the semi-local Shapiro–Mackey description $H^2(G, \mathrm{Res}_r\,\mathrm{CoInd}_U^\Gamma V) \cong \bigoplus_{t \in T} H^2(D, V)$ obtained from Mackey's decomposition and Shapiro's lemma for the subgroup $D = r^{-1}(U)$ of $G$. It is used in the construction of global level-constant $2$-cocycles with prescribed local restrictions, via [`groupCohomology.exists_forall_locRes_continuousH2S_coind_trivial_eq_add_smul`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_forall_locRes_continuousH2S_coind_trivial_eq_add_smul).
